[7]{8x+11})^{7} & ={1}^{7} \\\\ 8x+11 & =1 \\\\ 8x & =-10 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-\\frac{5}{4}.$"} :step/id #uuid "cffb8717-3bdb-52ea-babd-1b0ede29507c"}] :activity/title "Roots of Transformed Radical Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572313}]}
